# Authenticators and identifiers

## Plugin semantics

Authenticators extract credentials (form, session, token, …). Identifiers resolve those credentials to an identity (password identifier, etc.).

## Required behavior

- Add authenticators/identifiers using documented class names and config for the installed major.
- Keep field maps (`username`/`password`) aligned with forms and Table schema.
- Test login success, failure, and logout paths.

## Anti-patterns

- Custom credential parsing that bypasses authenticators without need
- Hard-coding secrets in authenticator config committed to git
